cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the archived repository."
title: "Average coverage is not enough: per-facility reliable conformal prediction for urban parking-occupancy forecasting — replication package"
authors:
  - family-names: Abdelmagid
    given-names: Mohamed
    affiliation: "Khalifa University, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates"
    email: 100059835@ku.ac.ae
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a study evaluating seven interval-forecasting methods on 50 parking
  facilities in two cities under a delay-aware protocol, introducing a two-level evaluation standard
  that separates population-level validity from per-facility validity. Code MIT; Birmingham-derived
  data CC BY 4.0; Belgrade data not redistributed (see DATA_AVAILABILITY.md).
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - prediction intervals
  - parking occupancy
  - intelligent transportation systems
license: MIT
type: software
